On Fri, Sep 19, 2003 at 03:58:20PM +0200, Hegedus, Ervin wrote:
> i put it a "make all" command, but i didn't find bootable kernel...

Use 'make boot'. Other than that, everything works just like in the
x86-based platforms (i.e. make modules, etc.). The kernel image will
reside in arch/alpha/boot/vmlinuz. Booting this image depends on your
computer's boot process (i.e. SRM vs. AlphaBios/Milo etc.). Check the
relevant docs for that subject or come back to the list.

