On Sunday 21 September 2003 08:58 pm, Jean-S=E9bastien Guay wrote:
> So my question is, why is the latest kernel giving me only 5
> MBPS? Is there a configuration setting I need to turn on in
> the kernel or in some config file? I tried looking around, but
> I can't find anything specific to my particular
> circumstances...

What SCSI controller are you using?  Each SCSI HBA driver has=20
different options.  Some have options for forcing a certain=20
speed.

Also, what module did your Debian kernel use for the SCSI driver,=20
and what module does your new 2.4.22 kernel use?  Some cards=20
(like SymBIOS/NCR and QLogic cards) have multiple possible=20
drivers to choose from.  It's quite likely that in those cases,=20
one driver will work better for you than another.

=2D-=20
Kelledin
