On 24 Sep 2003 09:07:51 +0200
Bourdin Pierre <bourdin@imerir.com> wrote:


> I'll try the middle button ? (The one with a triangle in the circle ?)
> Do you press it at any moment ?
Yes, the middle button, it's also called the stop button. It stops in
SRM. You can press it any time and it goes to SRM (even after a kernel
panic). It's an "on" or "off" state button, so when you boot again, you
don't forget to switch it off again (maybe there is a green light
telling it's in stop mode).

Greetings, Adrian.




